This repository is the test suite for Msgcore and TargetCore. It contains no
library code of its own, and it cannot be built on its own -- see the
"Components required at build time" section below, which is not a formality
here: three of the components named there have no public remote at all.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attribution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every file in this repository is the work of Khrustal & Mann, unlike the two
libraries it tests -- Msgcore and TargetCore are jointly attributed to Ivyware
Pty Ltd and Khrustal & Mann, because they carry Ivyware code dating to 2000.
Nothing of that lineage is reproduced here.

One qualification, recorded because the opposite assumption is the natural one.
The Msgcore suite exercises the same library surface that the older, ad-hoc
smoke program MsgcoreTests/MsgcoreTests.cpp touched, and its case list was
informed by that program. It is not a copy of it: MsgcoreTests.cpp is 434 lines
of unasserted console output and carries no copyright notice of its own;
MsgcoreSuite.cpp is 1224 lines of named, asserted cases. The attribution above
reflects that, and follows the same reading applied in _TargetCore_UseExamples,
whose harnesses have the same relationship to their Ivyware-era ancestors.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files that carry no licence header
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The reason in each case is mechanical rather than legal. All of these ARE
covered by the Apache License, Version 2.0:

    golden_ref.p2p              A serialised P2Pmsg heap image -- binary, and
                                the byte-identical cross-OS reference that the
                                golden_utf16_bytes test compares against with
                                cmake -E compare_files. Any header text would
                                be part of the comparison and would fail it.
                                Marked `binary` in .gitattributes for the
                                related reason (EOL translation would corrupt
                                it on checkout).

    .gitattributes              Git configuration, consumed by Git's own
    .gitignore                  parsers; carried without headers here as in the
                                sibling repositories.

Note on vectors/*.vec. These DO carry a short notice, but it is written by the
emitter (seal_interop.cpp, the `emit` mode) rather than added to the files by
hand. They are regenerated on each backend -- Windows CNG and Linux OpenSSL --
so a notice edited into a checked-in vector is erased the next time that vector
is refreshed, without anybody having touched the file. The emitted form is the
short one because the vector is data, and because its reader (ReadVector, at
seal_interop.cpp:185) skips '#' lines wholesale.


